#: ../../source/guides/first-app/static_pages.rst:125
msgid "Adding Logic to the Controller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/first-app/static_pages.rst:128
msgid "Create home.php and about.php"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/first-app/static_pages.rst:130
msgid ""
"Earlier you set up a controller with a ``view()`` method. The method "
"accepts one parameter, which is the name of the page to be loaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/first-app/static_pages.rst:133
msgid ""
"The static page bodies will be located in the **app/Views/pages** "
"directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/first-app/static_pages.rst:135
msgid ""
"In that directory, create two files named **home.php** and **about.php**."
" Within those files, type some text - anything you'd like - and save "
"them. If you like to be particularly un-original, try \"Hello World!\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/first-app/static_pages.rst:140
msgid "Complete Pages::view() Method"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/first-app/static_pages.rst:142
msgid ""
"In order to load those pages, you'll have to check whether the requested "
"page actually exists. This will be the body of the ``view()`` method in "
"the ``Pages`` controller created above:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/first-app/static_pages.rst:148
msgid ""
"And add ``use CodeIgniter\\Exceptions\\PageNotFoundException;`` after the"
" ``namespace`` line to import the ``PageNotFoundException`` class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/first-app/static_pages.rst:151
msgid ""
"Now, when the requested page does exist, it is loaded, including the "
"header and footer, and returned to the user. If a controller returns a "
"string, it is displayed to the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/first-app/static_pages.rst:155
msgid ""
"Controllers must return a string or a :doc:`Response "
"<../../outgoing/response>` object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/first-app/static_pages.rst:157
msgid ""
"If the requested page doesn't exist, a \"404 Page not found\" error is "
"shown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/first-app/static_pages.rst:159
msgid ""
"The first line in this method checks whether the page actually exists. "
"PHP's native ``is_file()`` function is used to check whether the file is "
"where it's expected to be. The ``PageNotFoundException`` is a CodeIgniter"
" exception that causes the 404 Page Not Found error page to show."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/first-app/static_pages.rst:164
msgid ""
"In the header template, the ``$title`` variable was used to customize the"
" page title. The value of title is defined in this method, but instead of"
" assigning the value to a variable, it is assigned to the title element "
"in the ``$data`` array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/first-app/static_pages.rst:169
msgid ""
"The last thing that has to be done is loading the views in the order they"
" should be displayed. The :php:func:`view()` function built-in to "
"CodeIgniter will be used to do this. The second parameter in the "
"``view()`` function is used to pass values to the view. Each value in the"
" ``$data`` array is assigned to a variable with the name of its key. So "
"the value of ``$data['title']`` in the controller is equivalent to "
"``$title`` in the view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/first-app/static_pages.rst:177
msgid ""
"Any files and directory names passed into the :php:func:`view()` function"
" MUST match the case of the actual directory and file itself or the "
"system will throw errors on case-sensitive platforms. You can read more "
"about it in :doc:`../../outgoing/views`."
msgstr ""

